    "test_commit": "bc8d66d538931e650dd2855fabe768720dcb4b02",
    "problem_statement": "In the RTIO framework, a callback operation placed in a chain of submissions is not invoked when an earlier submission in that chain fails, and even when it is invoked it has no way to learn about the failure. As a result, a callback at the end of a chain is silently skipped after a preceding error, and there is no way for it to observe the result code of the operation that failed. The desired behaviour is that a callback in a chain is always invoked regardless of the success or error status of the earlier submissions in the chain, and that it is given the result code of the first error in the chain so the application can react to bus-controller failures asynchronously.",
